---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Crumbs from '../components/Crumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
import { crumbLd, webPageLd } from '../lib/ld';

const crumbs = [{ name: 'Contact', path: '/contact/' }];
const desc = `Send spec corrections and questions to ${SITE.email}. The contact form opens your email app. This page does not store the message.`;
const jsonld = [webPageLd('Contact TreadmillSpecs.com', '/contact/', desc, SITE.checked), crumbLd(crumbs), { '@type': 'ContactPage', name: 'Contact', url: SITE.url + '/contact/' }];
---
<Base title="Contact TreadmillSpecs.com" description={desc} path="/contact/" nav="about" og="/og/page-contact.png" jsonld={jsonld}>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <div class="pagehead">
      <Crumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
      <h1>Contact</h1>
      <p class="lede">Corrections are welcome. A link to the manufacturer page, and the figure you think is wrong, is the fastest way to get a row fixed.</p>
    </div>
    <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. That is the only address for this site. There is no phone line and no staff directory. Mail keeps a written record a correction can be checked against.</p>
    <h2>What a correction should include</h2>
    <p>Name the model, quote the figure on this site, and link the manufacturer page or manual that prints a different figure. A photo of a spec sticker on a machine you own is useful context, and it is not a substitute for the maker’s page. Rows are filled from the manufacturer, not from a retailer listing, a review, or another model year.</p>
    <p>A missing cell that says “Not published by manufacturer” changes only when the cited page, or that maker’s manual, states the field. Deck thickness will not be entered as step-up height. Incline levels will not be converted to a percent. A horsepower number that appears only in a store title stays out of the table.</p>
    <h2>What this form does</h2>
    <p>The form below opens your own email program, addressed to {SITE.email}. This page does not receive the message, does not store it, and does not add you to a list. If your mail app does not open, copy the address and send the note yourself.</p>
    <p>Price-drop reminder requests are a different form, on each model page. That form can store an email. It does not send mail. The privacy page describes what is stored. Do not send a password, a payment card, or a medical history. This site cannot look up an order, because it does not sell treadmills.</p>
    <form class="stack" action={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} method="post" enctype="text/plain">
      <label for="cName">Your name</label>
      <input id="cName" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" />
      <label for="cEmail">Your email</label>
      <input id="cEmail" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" />
      <label for="cMsg">Message</label>
      <textarea id="cMsg" name="message" rows="6" placeholder="Model, the figure, and the manufacturer URL."></textarea>
      <button class="primary" type="submit">Open in my email app</button>
      <p class="small muted">This opens a message to {SITE.email} in your mail app. Nothing is stored by this page.</p>
    </form>
  </div>
</Base>
